WEEK 2 | Commit 14

CHANGES:
- New PATCH /api/user/settings BFF route for persisting user preferences to backend
- Updated feedback BFF route with expanded category validation matching all frontend modals

DETAILS:
- User settings route: Proxies to backend PATCH /api/user/settings with JWT from cookie
- Accepts { preferred_lang, theme } payload and returns success/error response
- Requires authentication: returns 401 Unauthorized if no rumi_token cookie present
- Enables Profile page Save Changes button to persist preferences to database
- Feedback route type validation expanded:
  - Before: Only accepted 'up', 'down', 'report' types (3 categories)
  - After: Accepts general, bug, feature, appreciation, incorrect, offensive, ocr_error, other
- Feedback route: session_id and message_id now passed as optional to backend
- Enables both navbar general feedback (no chat context) and chat message-specific reports
- Error handling consistent with other BFF routes using jsonError() helper

FILES: src/app/api/user/settings/route.ts (new), src/app/api/feedback/route.ts
